# Fixture for reactant_count_helper_test: one helper read by two rules with
# different reactant counts (issue #59).  The A rule names g() as its whole
# rate law; the B rule reads it through _rateLaw1 = 3*g().  g() has a single
# slot, so RM priced the B rule off the A rule's count, which is a wrong rate
# rather than a zero one: B drained at 3*k*Aoff.
# Under TotalRate each A(s~0) flips at rate k and each B(s~0) at rate 3k, so
# Aoff(t) is binomial(100, exp(-k t)) and Boff(t) binomial(50, exp(-3 k t)).
begin model
begin parameters
  k 1e-2
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(s~0~1)
  B(s~0~1)
end molecule types
begin species
  A(s~0) 100
  B(s~0) 50
end species
begin observables
  Molecules Aoff A(s~0)
  Molecules Boff B(s~0)
end observables
begin functions
  reactant_1()
  g() = reactant_1()*k
end functions
begin reaction rules
  A(s~0) -> A(s~1)  g() TotalRate
  B(s~0) -> B(s~1)  3*g() TotalRate
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML()
end actions
